---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NewsletterSignup from '../components/NewsletterSignup.astro';
import { posts } from '../data/posts';
const examples = posts.slice(0, 3);
---

<BaseLayout wide title="Glenn Edley | MondayMotivator, writing and work" description="Kickstart your thinking with MondayMotivator, Glenn Edley's weekly email. Read the archive, explore his work, or find help with your customer communication.">
  <main>
    <section class="home-hero" aria-labelledby="home-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">MondayMotivator · Since 2004</p>
        <h1 id="home-title">Kickstart<br />your thinking<br /><span>and your week.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-description">A fresh thought, a useful question or a story that helps you see things differently. Get my MondayMotivator in your inbox each week.</p>
        <NewsletterSignup id="home-mondaymotivator" />
        <p class="hero-note">Free to read. <a href="/mondaymotivator/">Explore the archive first.</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-note-block">
        <p class="eyebrow">A note from Glenn</p>
        <p class="hero-statement">Life gives us<br />plenty to<br />think about.</p>
        <p>I write about what I'm learning in life and business, the habits we build, and the things that make us stop and think.</p>
        <p>MondayMotivator is where I bring those thoughts together.</p>
        <a href="/mondaymotivator/">More of my writing <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="reading-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Start reading</p><h2 id="reading-title">Something to think about.</h2></div><a href="/mondaymotivator/">Browse the archive →</a></div>
      <ol class="reading-grid">
        {examples.map((post, index) => <li><span class="reading-number">0{index + 1}</span><h3><a href={`/mondaymotivator/${post.year}/${post.slug}/`}>{post.title}</a></h3><a class="small-link" href={`/mondaymotivator/${post.year}/${post.slug}/`}>Read this edition →</a></li>)}
      </ol>
      <p class="section-note">You can also explore the archive through <a href="/four-factors/">the Four Factors</a>: Belief, Programming the Mind, Mental Posture and Focus.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section about-section" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">The person behind the emails</p><h2 id="about-title">I'm Glenn.</h2></div>
      <div><p>I'm a writer, a business owner, a husband and a dad. I like good questions, getting things done and a round of disc golf.</p><p>I founded <a href="/work-with-spike/">Spike</a> and have spent more than 20 years helping businesses communicate with their customers. I also lead marketing for <a href="https://racerproducts.co.nz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Racer Products</a> and <a href="https://scarles.co.nz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Scarles</a>.</p><p>That experience is part of what I write about. So is the rest of life.</p><a class="small-link" href="/now/">What I'm doing now →</a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">When you want help</p><h2 id="work-title">Two ways to work together.</h2></div></div>
      <div class="work-grid">
        <article><p class="eyebrow">Advice and direction</p><h3>Work with Glenn</h3><p>You want a fresh pair of eyes on your business, your customer communication or where sales are getting stuck. We'll start with what's happening and what you're trying to change.</p><a class="text-action" href="/your-next-move/">Explore working with Glenn →</a></article>
        <article><p class="eyebrow">Email marketing done for you</p><h3>Work with Spike</h3><p>You want your email marketing planned and handled. Spike is my agency, helping businesses with Mailchimp, campaigns and customer email.</p><a class="text-action" href="/work-with-spike/">Explore working with Spike →</a></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section projects-section" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Elsewhere in my work</p><h2 id="projects-title">Writing, ideas and projects.</h2>
      <ul class="project-list"><li><a href="/light-your-own-fire/">Light Your Own Fire <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><p>The book I co-wrote with Charles Donoghue.</p></li><li><a href="/the-swearing-project/">The Swearing Project <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><p>A short, honest guide to finding the pause before you react.</p></li><li><a href="/articles-and-media/">Articles &amp; Media <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><p>Masterclasses, podcast appearances and articles in one place.</p></li></ul>
      <details class="old-habits"><summary>Why the old site was #efefef</summary><p>When I first started building emails they were tables within tables with the simplest HTML possible, and the background colour was almost always #efefef. Simple code is still the best way to have your emails render properly and improve your deliverability.</p><p>Old habits die hard. Some of them are good.</p></details>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
